<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96274" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στᾰσι-ώτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					111
				</span></i>
			) mostly in pl., <i>members of a party</i> or <i>faction in
				a state, partisans</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τοῦ
				Μεγακλέος ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.60
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				59
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				173
			</span></i>, al.; acting as <i>a body-guard</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. (with
			punning allusion to 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					1.1
				</span></i>
			), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τοῦ ὅλου ς</span>. the
				<i>partisans</i> of 'The Whole', opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ῥέοντες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				181a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῆς φύσεως καὶ
			ἀφυσίκους</span>, of Parmenides and Melissus, who denied
			motion, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				10.46
			</span></i>.</div>
